==Battleground==
*1 [[Festival Sign Girl]] spawns as the boss after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*5 [[Doge Dark]]s (200%) spawn after 16 seconds<sup>480f</sup>, delay 7~12.67 seconds<sup>210f~380f</sup>.
*5 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn after 25.67 seconds<sup>770f</sup>, delay 9~13.33 seconds<sup>270f~400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Doge Dark]] (10%) spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 7~14 seconds<sup>210f~420f</sup>.
**1 [[Vendor El]] spawns.
**1 [[Owlbrow]] spawns.
**3 [[Duche]]s spawn, delay 9~15.67 seconds<sup>270f~470f</sup>.
**6 [[Duche]]s spawn, delay 25 seconds<sup>750f</sup>.
**3 [[Shadow Boxer K]]s spawn, delay 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>.
**2 [[Vendor El]]s spawn, delay 23 seconds<sup>690f</sup>.
**1 [[Duche]] spawns.
**2 [[Vendor El]]s spawn, delay 15.33~23.33 seconds<sup>460f~700f</sup>.
**2 [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**2 [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**2 [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 1 second<sup>30f</sup>.
**2 [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 0.67 seconds<sup>20f</sup>.
**1 [[Doge Dark]] (200%) spawns.
**1 [[Vendor El]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Even with 5 Vendor Els, they lack the ability to push. Instead, the real threat are the Shadow Boxer K, who can push the Vendor Els into range of your [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]]. Spam meatshields, and [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]], since Paris is very helpful to handle the Shadow Boxers.

==='''Strategy 1 (~30 second speedrun)'''===
{{Lineup
|Richest Cat
|Jiangshi Cat
|Li'l King Dragon Cat
|Neo Cutter Cat
|Li'l Dark Cat
|Manic Lion Cat|30
|Green Shell Cat|30
|Bullet Train Cat|30
|Awakened Bahamut Cat|40
|talent9 = Explosion Lv. 10, Move Speed Up Lv. 10
|notes = This strategy still works without Awakened Bahamut Cat's Move Speed Up Talent, but its execution is extremely tight. The timing on Green Shell Cat must also be adjusted to slightly before Bahamut hits Doge Dark #2, and both Manic Lion Cat as well as Bullet Train Cat need to be spammed off cooldown in order to protect Bahamut. 
}}

'''Battle:''' Wait until you hit 3,000¢, then send out Bullet Train Cat to kill Festival Sign Girl. With the cash she drops, summon Talented Awakened Bahamut Cat instantly to kill Doge Dark, who should subsequently trigger the boss wave. The moment Bahamut hits Doge Dark #2, send out Green Shell Cat, as he will narrowly intercept the stack of Vender Els, letting Bahamut knock all of them behind the enemy base. Start spamming Manic Lion Cats at this point; they will protect Bahamut up until you clear the stage.

